{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/112548-help-me-stat-this-character-please","id":112548,"title":"Help me stat this character!!! Please!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-14T05:07:46-07:00","id":112548,"title":"Help me stat this character!!! Please!","content":"This is a character for a high power campaign. He's starting at Wyrd 5, he's also starting with four dots in Striking-Looks, several languages, and the Encyclopedic Knowledge merit.<br /> <br /> <br /> This character was an Irish American (Aidan) college student, a Classics Major, and basically a big blonde, blue-eyed, good-looking Bookworm, which is why his Keeper snatched him to be a Library Lamp. He was a Fairest/Bright-One for an long time, sitting around, ligthing up the library, reading. An Antiquarian came by one day and snobbishly asked what he was doing. In his best Irish brogue he said, &quot;I'm a reading Lamp. What should I do?&quot; Between the snappy answer and the silly delivery the Darkling laughed. That started a Friendship.<br /> <br /> <br /> Durring the years in the Library the two friends made a discovery of how to take on more Kiths (the technique works only in Arcadia). With some low cunning and high treason they worked out an escape plan and took most of the Library staff with them! Durring the crossing of the Hedge the group got seperated. Aidan, got the stragglers to the border then went back to delay the Keeper's enforcers. Aiden no longer remembers what he did, but he assumes it worked. Aidan then steped out of the Hedge, eighty years late! His friend the Antiquarian was there to meet him, and Oracle found out when he would get out, but she died soon after.<br /> <br /> <br /> Aidan has more Kiths than his Wyrd should support, this causes him problems. His Kiths are Bright-One, Flamesiren, Antiquarian, and Author. He has a problem like the Sureal Quality flaw from Changeling: the Dreaming in that all the crazies find him fascinating. That reflects his Bright-One and Flamesiren Kiths. He also talks like he was fed on dictionaries all his life and can't speak informally, which reflects the other two kiths.<br /> <br /> Aiden is a member of the Spring Court and has Court Goodwill from the Autumn and South Courts (this is San Francisco and the Directional Courts are in the mix). Aiden was born in the 19th century, but came out of the Hedge in 2010 looking like a College kid. Aiden is exceptionally tall (6ft.5in.) and athletically built. Aiden is allied with the Scarecrow Ministry and does both social engineering and propoganda work for them.<br /> <br /> (more later).<br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-14-2014, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T08:49:11-07:00","id":112676,"title":"","content":"Wow.<br /> <br /> So, like, how much experience are you being given to build this dude? Which rules variant is your GM using for multiple kiths? Honestly, though, you probably don't need all those kiths. You can easily simulate the Flamesiren kith + Surreal Quality by purchasing the Siren's Song merit found in Rites of Spring. After that, just keep the Antiquarian kith and drop Author ... doesn't seem as integral to your concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T11:50:28-07:00","id":112820,"title":"","content":"um, by the rules you can have only one extra kith (duel kith merit from Winter Masques) unless your storyteller allows more so i'm a bit confused as to how you have four.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T14:12:00-07:00","id":112925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/112548-help-me-stat-this-character-please?p=112676#post112676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow.<br /> So, like, how much experience are you being given to build this dude?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a question I'm asking you guys.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which rules variant is your GM using for multiple kiths? Honestly, though, you probably don't need all those kiths. </div> </div> </div>It's more a matter of having a Kith overload and problems with that. Basically he's damaged in a different way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can easily simulate the Flamesiren kith + Surreal Quality by purchasing the Siren's Song merit found in Rites of Spring. After that, just keep the Antiquarian kith and drop Author ... doesn't seem as integral to your concept. </div> </div> </div>Interesting idea about the Siren's Song Merit. But the guy is an Author in the sense that he writes books. He also uses his pen to perform propoganda for the Scarecrow Ministry.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T14:13:38-07:00","id":112926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lost_in_the_Hedge777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/112548-help-me-stat-this-character-please?p=112820#post112820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">um, by the rules you can have only one extra kith (duel kith merit from Winter Masques) unless your storyteller allows more so i'm a bit confused as to how you have four.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A trick that works only in Arcadia, and with as low a Wyrd as my character has, it has side effects. All the PCs in the game are supposed to be interestingly damaged but powerful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T18:19:29-07:00","id":113047,"title":"","content":"Uh. I don't understand. Did your GM not assign to you a number of experience points with which to build your characters? If this isn't an issue, why do you need our advice? Just assign whatever numbers you feel thematically appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T23:59:38-07:00","id":113166,"title":"","content":"Good lord that's a lot of kiths. But when it comes to stating this guy out I'm at a loss. We don't really need your backstory, we need what you want to do with this guy. Is he a scholar of fae lore? A daring hero delving the deep dark ruins of the hedge? An indolent layabout?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T04:25:55-07:00","id":113238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/112548-help-me-stat-this-character-please?p=113047#post113047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uh. I don't understand. Did your GM not assign to you a number of experience points with which to build your characters? If this isn't an issue, why do you need our advice? Just assign whatever numbers you feel thematically appropriate.</div> </div> </div> </div>No he didn't he wants us to come up with warped concepts and work them out. The group is to be freaks amoung the freaks. Two of the other characters have taken two Seemings, A Fairest/Beast and a Fairest/Ogre.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T04:36:56-07:00","id":113241,"title":"","content":"He basically works for the Spring Court and the Scarecrow Ministry ( The Spring, Autumn, and Southern Courts are closely allied in this campaign). He is a scholar and an author. He writes fiction for a living (Sci fi and Ghost stories mainly) and he also writes non-fiction which aides the Scarecrow Ministry's agendas. Example: &quot;While the reports of a monster in the area are clearly cheap dull hokum, the area is known to have several nasty criminal gangs in it. Those looking for supernatural thrills should go elsewhere.&quot; I.e. he manipulaates thrillseekers away from the dangerous places and creats alternitive reasons to fear going to these areas. He also works as a &quot;Social Engineer&quot; the guy is both extraordinarily good-looking and very charming, added to that he genuinely likes people and wants them to be happy. He's very good a seducing people and far better at getting them to seduce him. He often used his charms to build peoples confidence (and not always or mainly in sexual ways).<br /> Added to that. He is a very learned scholar who has high physical stats. He does do some of the darring do stuff. However, you've got to get his nose out of a book first.<br /> <br /> Does any of this help you out Sir Pants.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-15-2014, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T08:31:24-07:00","id":113348,"title":"","content":"Need two more things, what's the exp budget and what is your character bad at?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1266-sirpants","name":"SirPants","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T14:21:03-07:00","id":113555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SirPants</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/112548-help-me-stat-this-character-please?p=113348#post113348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Need two more things, what's the exp budget and what is your character bad at?</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked about this twice. Apparently, there is no budget and his GM is cool with him &quot;working it out.&quot; Which means basically anything goes, rules-wise. I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T03:07:55-07:00","id":113942,"title":"","content":"You should check out the Dawn book, it has an entitlement called The pilgrims of the Endless Road, they are all about changing themselves to gain more power. Their blessing allows them to gain another seaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T04:43:20-07:00","id":113966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SirPants</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/112548-help-me-stat-this-character-please?p=113348#post113348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Need two more things, what's the exp budget and what is your character bad at?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The &quot;budget&quot; is that everybody gets a role, and the other PCs don't trip on it. I'm the generalist, I don't challenge anybody else's specialist roles. I'm large strong, agile, and enduring, but I have few fighting skills. I'm charming, but I strange and have serious social handicaps. I'm learned and highly intellegent, but I lack focus. Picture a character that's a cross between the Professor and Ginger from Giligan's Island. Yes, he widely competent, but his sheer level of quirkiness also limits him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T04:45:26-07:00","id":113968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/112548-help-me-stat-this-character-please?p=113555#post113555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I asked about this twice. Apparently, there is no budget and his GM is cool with him &quot;working it out.&quot; Which means basically anything goes, rules-wise. I think.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The rule is everybody gets their role. My role is generalist. We've got a Witch, a Fixer, a Warrior Beast, a Noble Soldier, and a Jester/Trickster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T04:50:05-07:00","id":113969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lost_in_the_Hedge777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/112548-help-me-stat-this-character-please?p=112820#post112820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">um, by the rules you can have only one extra kith (duel kith merit from Winter Masques) unless your storyteller allows more so i'm a bit confused as to how you have four.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Having looks at the Siren song Merit, it's interesting, but doesn't fit. What do you guys think about reworking the Enchanting Performance Merit to work with Socialise? Basically Aiden socialises with people and he is able to make them feel very good and deeply flattered. Aiden's presence would be magically soothing and confidence building. People would feel that he had seen their inner beauty, and that in his eyes they were truely beautiful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}